    "background_story": "Forest, a vast and ancient woodland, was a tapestry of diverse ecosystems. Despite its name, Forest was far from uniform, with varied landscapes and microclimates that supported a wide range of flora and fauna. The north side of Forest was dominated by towering conifers, while the south side was home to deciduous trees that burst into vibrant colors each autumn. The terrain itself was a mix of rolling hills, sparkling streams, and rocky outcroppings. This inhomogeneity created a rich mosaic of habitats, allowing Forest to support an incredible array of wildlife, from the majestic elk to the tiny, iridescent dragonflies. As a result, Forest was a haven for scientists and naturalists, who came to study and marvel at the intricate web of life that thrived within its borders.",
